74 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 57 0 R
/T (Small agencies and freelancers already do their client work in chat. Drafts go out as screenshots on WhatsApp, and feedback comes back as a mix of short texts, long voice notes in Hindi or Hinglish, and replies from several people at the client. Nobody keeps a reliable list of what was actually asked, contradictions surface late, the next version quietly misses a change, and when a dispute comes up there is no clear record of who approved what.)
/E (Small agencies and freelancers already do their client work in chat. Drafts go out as screenshots on WhatsApp, and feedback comes back as a mix of short texts, long voice notes in Hindi or Hinglish, and replies from several people at the client. Nobody keeps a reliable list of what was actually asked, contradictions surface late, the next version quietly misses a change, and when a dispute comes up there is no clear record of who approved what.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
75 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 57 0 R
/T (Approval portals already exist, and "no-login approval links" are now standard. What doesn't exist as a simple product is a tool that works inside the conversation itself: one that listens to the chat the client is already having, turns it into a checklist the team can act on, and catches drift before work ships. Drifty was built to be that room, using Nexconn for every conversation.)
/E (Approval portals already exist, and "no-login approval links" are now standard. What doesn't exist as a simple product is a tool that works inside the conversation itself: one that listens to the chat the client is already having, turns it into a checklist the team can act on, and catches drift before work ships. Drifty was built to be that room, using Nexconn for every conversation.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
