958 0 obj
<<
/Title (Small agencies and freelancers already do their client work in chat. Drafts go out as screenshots on WhatsApp, and feedback comes back as a mix of short texts, long voice notes in Hindi or Hinglish, and replies from several people at the client. Nobody keeps a reliable list of what was actually asked, contradictions surface late, the next version quietly misses a change, and when a dispute comes up there is no clear record of who approved what.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 592 0 R
/Next 959 0 R
>>
endobj
959 0 obj
<<
/Title (Approval portals already exist, and "no-login approval links" are now standard. What doesn't exist as a simple product is a tool that works inside the conversation itself: one that listens to the chat the client is already having, turns it into a checklist the team can act on, and catches drift before work ships. Drifty was built to be that room, using Nexconn for every conversation.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 592 0 R
/Prev 958 0 R
>>
endobj
